The generated Lev1, Lev1T, Lev2 and Lev2T parametric descriptions are retained
with package renaming. LevenshteinAutomata retains Lucene's parametric state
and bit-unpacking logic, adapted to evaluate Unicode transitions on demand.
TermDictionary supplies Datalevin's UTF-8 radix-trie intersection.

The levenshtein automata tables (under core/src/java/org/apache/lucene/util/automaton) were
automatically generated with the moman/finenight FSA library, created by
Jean-Philippe Barrette-LaPierre. This library is available under an MIT license,
see http://sites.google.com/site/rrettesite/moman and
http://bitbucket.org/jpbarrette/moman/overview/

